    "reply": "Cystic fibrosis is linked to several specific genes [2]. The condition is associated with NCBIGene:1080 [1]. Genetic associations also include NCBIGene:2212 and NCBIGene:7040 [3][4].\n\n## Associated Genes\n\nThe primary entity implicated is NCBIGene:1080 [1]. Another relevant locus identified is NCBIGene:2212 [3]. In addition, the disorder is linked to NCBIGene:7040 [4].\n\n## Clinical Manifestations\n\nA documented clinical feature of the disease is Bronchiectasis [15]. Affected individuals may also present with Dehydration [23]. Other recognized manifestations include Diarrhea as well as Hemoptysis [27][28].\n\n## Hepatic Complications\n\nHepatosplenomegaly is recognized among the clinical features [30]. Liver involvement impacts a substantial subset of patients, but brain dysfunction remains an uncommon consequence [26: \"Cystic fibrosis liver disease (CFLD) affects a large proportion of cystic fibrosis (CF) patients; however encephalopathy is a rare complication\"]. Furthermore, increased ammonia levels causing encephalopathy may be induced by systemic steroid treatment [26: \"hyperammonemic encephalopathy\\\" can be precipitated in previously stable CFLD by various triggers including systemic corticosteroids\"].",
    "dur": 3.495
   },
   {
