    "openrouter_cost_usd": 0.0109485,
    "reply": "Genetic analysis identifies CF transmembrane conductance regulator as an associated locus [1]. In addition, Fc gamma receptor IIa is implicated [3]. The gene transforming growth factor beta 1 is also linked to the pathology [4].\n\n## Associated Disease Characteristics\nThe primary condition is Cystic fibrosis [2]. A related title appears as Cystic fibrosis [6]. The literature entity is Cystic Fibrosis [7]. A clinical trial evaluates Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [8]. Another study assesses Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [24]. \n\n## Clinical Presentation\nCystic fibrosis features include Asthma [11]. Documented manifestations comprise Bronchiectasis [15]. Physical signs include Clubbing of fingers [19]. Other documented symptoms include Dehydration [23]. Patients also exhibit Diarrhea [27]. Respiratory complications include Hemoptysis [28]. Abdominal signs include Hepatomegaly [29]. Clinical evaluation also notes Hepatosplenomegaly [30].\n\n## Published Literature\nThe literature includes Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis [5]. Publication citations list 32800451 [9]. Publications also address 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis [10]. Another source is 35240644 [13]. Other editorial work covers Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children [14]. Additional research is indexed under 35592838 [17]. Therapeutic articles discuss Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis [18]. Further documentation is found under 35853636 [21]. Endocrine studies feature Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes [22]. Subsequent work is recorded in 39129918 [25]. In advanced liver involvement, severe neurological symptoms can emerge [26: \"encephalopathy is a rare complication\"].\n\n## Additional Studies\nTrials investigate A Study of Topical Danazol for the Treatment of Pain Associated With Fibrocystic Breast Disease [12]. Complementary trials include Efficacy and Safety of ONCOXIN in Patients With Breast Fibrocystic Disease [16]. Other interventions examine A Clinical Study on the Efficacy and Safety of the Treatment of Hyperplasia of Mammary Glands With Xiaoru Sanjie Capsule [20].",
    "dur": 5.122
